        <history>
          <p>Written while Nielsen was staying in Athens, the Helios Overture depicts sunrise to sunset over the Aegean Sea. Nielsen inscribed the score with Greek text describing the sun's journey, and the work's broad orchestral arc from silence to full brilliance and back has made it one of his most popular concert openers.</p>
